# The image needs exactly two files. Everything else — tests, docs, the
# screenshot, .git — was being shipped to the Docker daemon on every build for
# no reason. Deny-all then allow, so adding a file to the repo cannot silently
# bloat the context again.
#
# If you add a COPY to the Dockerfile, add an exception for it here too, or the
# build fails with "file not found" despite the file plainly existing.
*
!requirements.txt
!app.py
